        },
        "parms": "# dict.serialize, dict.deserialize and dict.print — dictionaries as text\ndict.serialize sends a dictionary as one line of JSON: :: keys become nested objects and a value of several numbers an array. dict.deserialize reads such a line into the dictionary it names, replacing what it held, and sends its reference one audio block later. dict.print writes a dictionary to the log as indented JSON, each line starting with its name.\nA message holds at most 255 characters; for more, send write song.json to dict.serialize and read song.json to dict.deserialize, which use a file of up to 128 KiB. Unlike Max, the JSON leaves as a message, not a dictionary, and deserialized keys come in alphabetical order (yse-soundengine#1243).",
        "type": ".text"
      },
